  "content": "# Supervised vs. Unsupervised Learning\n\n## Supervised Learning\nThink of it like **learning with a teacher who has an answer key**.\n\n- You give the model **data that already has answers** (labels)\n- Example: Photos labeled \"cat\" or \"dog\" — the model learns the patterns connecting images to labels\n- Goal: Predict correct answers for **new, unseen data**\n- Common tasks: Spam detection, price prediction, medical diagnosis\n\n## Unsupervised Learning\nThink of it like **finding patterns without any answer key**.\n\n- You give the model **raw data with no labels**\n- The model must discover hidden structures on its own\n- Example: Given customer purchase data, it might group customers into \"budget shoppers\" and \"premium shoppers\" — groups you never defined\n- Common tasks: Customer segmentation, anomaly detection, recommendation systems\n\n## Quick Analogy 🧒\n- **Supervised**: A kid learning to sort fruit by watching a parent say \"this is an apple, this is an orange\" repeatedly.\n- **Unsupervised**: The same kid sorting a fruit basket alone — they might group by color, size, or shape without being told how.\n\n## Key Difference in One Line\n> Supervised",
